13.1 Victory Points (VP)
Victory Points represent strategic progress.
Players earn VP through objectives, combat achievements, territory control, and experimental milestones.

VP Sources
Capturing command zones

Destroying enemy command units

Completing objectives

Holding strategic terrain

Deploying experimental units

Completing recon sweeps

Winning VR missions

Maintaining logistics superiority

VP Thresholds
Different game modes use different VP thresholds:

Skirmish: 100 VP

Campaign: mission‑specific

Competitive: configurable

Modded: defined by scenario

VP Decay
Some VP sources decay over time:

Temporary objectives

Hazard‑affected zones

Disrupted command radius

VP ensures multiple paths to victory.

13.2 Objectives
Objectives define the strategic tasks players must complete to win.

Objective Types
Type	Description
Primary Objectives	Required to win; mission‑critical
Secondary Objectives	Optional; grant VP or bonuses
Dynamic Objectives	Change based on battlefield conditions
Secret Objectives	Hidden until triggered
VR Objectives	Completed in VR missions
Experimental Objectives	Related to superweapon deployment


Objective Examples
Capture and hold command zones

Destroy enemy Command Core

Complete recon sweep

Breach fortified structure

Escort logistics convoy

Deploy experimental unit

Survive hazard event

Complete VR dogfight mission

Objectives create structure and variety in every match.

13.3 Secret Objectives
Secret objectives add unpredictability and strategic depth.

Secret Objective Types
Hidden recon tasks

Covert sabotage

Stealth infiltration

Hazard manipulation

Experimental activation

VR operator missions

Secret Objective Rules
Revealed only when triggered

Provide large VP bonuses

May alter battlefield conditions

May unlock new abilities or units

Secret objectives reward adaptive play.

13.4 Elimination Rules
Elimination occurs when a player loses the ability to continue meaningful play.

Elimination Conditions
A player is eliminated when:

Command Core is destroyed

All command units are destroyed

No logistics nodes remain

No production buildings remain

No combat‑capable units remain

No experimental units remain (if required by scenario)

Elimination Effects
Command radius collapses

Token generation stops

Morale drops globally

Autonomous behavior becomes defensive

Remaining units attempt emergency retreat

Elimination is final unless revival mechanics are enabled.

13.5 Superweapon Victory
Experimental units and superweapons can create unique win conditions.

Superweapon Types
Gravity well

Energy storm

Quantum destabilizer

Terrain collapse

EMP blackout

Hazard field deployment

Superweapon Victory Conditions
A player wins if:

A superweapon is successfully deployed

The enemy Command Core is destroyed by experimental action

The battlefield is reshaped beyond enemy recovery

A quantum unit triggers a scenario‑specific victory event

Superweapon Rules
Require experimental resources

Require Vector Core activation

Require stable power grid

Require command unit presence

Have long cooldowns

Can be countered by enemy experimental units

Superweapon victories are rare, dramatic, and cinematic.

13.6 Campaign Victory
Campaign victory is determined by narrative progression.

Campaign Victory Types
Story Victory — complete all primary objectives

Branch Victory — choose one of multiple endings

Survival Victory — endure final mission

Experimental Victory — unlock and deploy final experimental unit

VR Victory — complete final VR mission chain

Campaign Loss Conditions
Command Core destroyed

Critical character death (if narrative‑based)

Logistics collapse

Failure of mission chain

Experimental failure event

Persistent Campaign Systems
Squad veterancy

Command unit upgrades

Tech tree progression

Resource carryover

VR mission unlocks

Experimental unit development

Campaign victory is designed to feel earned and consequential.
